# DESK42 side finding -- NOT a DESK42 behaviour: GEMDOS `Frename` accepts an
# EMPTY destination file name and writes a directory entry with an all-blank
# 8.3 name.
#
# The box's name field is emptied (11 x Backspace) and OK pressed.  EmuTOS's
# `inf_file_folder` has no empty-name special case either -- it unformats the
# field into `dstpth+nmidx` and calls `dos_rename(srcpth, dstpth)`, so with an
# empty field the destination is the bare directory `C:\`
# (deskinf.c:600-626).  EmuTOS's own GEMDOS refuses that
# (`xrename`: `if (!ixsfirst(p2,FA_SUBDIR,0)) return EACCDN`,
# bdos/fsdir.c:912-913); ours does not, and C:\README.TXT becomes an entry
# with no name at all.
#
#   D_EMPTY     the box with the name field emptied
#   E_AFTEROK   after OK -- no STRENAME, the window rebuilt, and the first file
#               icon has no label
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 38 35
1800 down
1803 up
1810 down
1813 up
2400 move 600 240
3200 mark B_WIN1
3600 move 179 271
4000 down
4003 up
4400 parkbr
5000 mark B2_FILESEL
5400 move 88 240
5600 move 88 9
6200 move 152 43
6800 down
7000 up
7600 parkbr
8600 mark C_FILEINFO
9000 key 0E
9020 key 8E
9080 key 0E
9100 key 8E
9160 key 0E
9180 key 8E
9240 key 0E
9260 key 8E
9320 key 0E
9340 key 8E
9400 key 0E
9420 key 8E
9480 key 0E
9500 key 8E
9560 key 0E
9580 key 8E
9640 key 0E
9660 key 8E
9720 key 0E
9740 key 8E
9800 key 0E
9820 key 8E
10400 mark D_EMPTY
10800 move 216 353
11200 down
11400 up
12000 parkbr
13000 mark E_AFTEROK
